 "notes": [
  "Theseus-GM[gt] starts at the ground-truth pose, so 100% success is a local-basin/preservation check, not global recovery.",
  "Theseus-GM[rand] is the informative Theseus number: it hits local minima at p>=0.3 (success 0.80/0.55/0.25).",
  "SDPR-SCS with W_i=I and unit weights minimises the same least-squares objective as Kabsch; paired per-trial errors agree to 1.5e-5 deg / 1.3e-9 m over 80 trials.  It is a correctness/availability check of the SDPR forward path, not an independent robust method.  A distinct SDPR baseline needs non-identity W_i (POLI) and/or a RANSAC front end.",
  "SCS forward failure rate was 0/208 across N=20/50/100 at eps=1e-9; failures at p>=0.3 are wrong poses, not exceptions.",
  "Pyatov/POLI/BPnP are out of scope for this 3D-3D table; see availability.md for exact reasons.",
  "Only 20 trials/cell: Wilson 95% CI for Theseus-GM[rand] at p=0.3/0.5/0.7 is [0.58,0.92]/[0.34,0.74]/[0.11,0.47].  GNC-GM is 20/20, CI [0.84,1.00]; p=0.3 intervals overlap, so the 16/20 vs 20/20 gap is not significant at 95%; p=0.5/0.7 are separated."
 ],
